.ad l
.TH kiinfo-kikvm 1 "8.0 - February 12, 2026" version "8.0"
.SH NAME
kiinfo  -  LinuxKI data collection and analysis engine

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiinfo \-kikvm [FLAGS] [OPTIONS]

.SH DESCRIPTION

\fBkiinfo -kikvm\fR generates the Docker Activity Report.  The report will provide a summary of CPU and IO statistics for the KVM guests, and then for each VM, the top tasks using User CPU, System CPU, waiting for CPU, and performing Disk IO are shown.   

.SH OPTIONS

See kiinfo(1).

.SH FLAGS
.B help
.RS
Provide help information for kikvm flags
.RE

.B npid=<npid>
.RS
Limit per-kvm guest details to list npids for each KVM guest
.RE

.B kvmtree
.RS
Create VIDS subdirectory with a file for each KVM guest VM.  Used with kiinfo -kparse kptree.
.RE

.B freq=<hc_per_sec>
.RS
CPU profile (hardclock) frequency (default 100 times per second)
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES

1) Create a KVM Activity Report and reporting the top 10 PIDs for each KVM guest: 

.B $ kiinfo -kikvm npid=10 -ts 1115_1758

